Source: linux-freedomnas
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: FreedomNAS Team <dev@freedomnas.io>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
 bc, bison, flex, cpio, file, kmod, rsync, xz-utils, zstd,
 dwarves, openssl, perl, python3,
 libelf-dev, libssl-dev, zlib1g-dev,
 rustc, rust-src, bindgen, libclang-dev,
 gawk, uuid-dev, libblkid-dev, libudev-dev, libaio-dev,
 libtirpc-dev, libpam0g-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://codeberg.org/FreedomNAS/linux-freedomnas
Vcs-Browser: https://codeberg.org/FreedomNAS/linux-freedomnas
Vcs-Git: https://codeberg.org/FreedomNAS/linux-freedomnas.git

Package: linux-image-@KREL@
Architecture: amd64
Depends: kmod, zfsutils-freedomnas (>= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: dracut, firmware-linux-free
Suggests: linux-headers-@KREL@
Conflicts: zfs-dkms
Provides: linux-image, wireguard-modules (= 1.0.0)
Description: FreedomNAS LTS Linux @KREL@ with OpenZFS
 The kernel and modules of Arch's linux-lts, built for Debian, with the
 OpenZFS @ZFSVER@ modules compiled in the same build and installed under
 extra/zfs. No DKMS: the kernel and its ZFS arrive together or not at all.

Package: linux-headers-@KREL@
Architecture: amd64
Depends: gcc, make, libc6-dev, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Headers for building modules for linux-image-@KREL@
 Headers, Kconfig files and build scripts for out-of-tree modules against
 the FreedomNAS kernel @KREL@.

Package: linux-image-freedomnas
Architecture: amd64
Depends: linux-image-@KREL@ (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: FreedomNAS LTS Linux with OpenZFS (latest)
 Depends on the newest FreedomNAS kernel, so installing this package keeps
 the system on it. Earlier kernels stay installed until removed.

Package: linux-headers-freedomnas
Architecture: amd64
Depends: linux-headers-@KREL@ (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Headers for the FreedomNAS kernel (latest)
 Depends on the headers of the newest FreedomNAS kernel.

Package: zfsutils-freedomnas
Section: admin
Architecture: amd64
Depends: gawk, python3, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: dracut
Provides: zfsutils, zfsutils-linux (= @ZFSVER@), zfs-zed (= @ZFSVER@),
 zfs-dracut (= @ZFSVER@), libpam-zfs (= @ZFSVER@),
 libnvpair3linux (= @ZFSVER@), libuutil3linux (= @ZFSVER@),
 libzfs7linux (= @ZFSVER@), libzpool7linux (= @ZFSVER@),
 libzfsbootenv1linux (= @ZFSVER@), libzfslinux-dev (= @ZFSVER@)
Conflicts: zfs-fuse, zfs-dkms, zfs-initramfs, zfsutils-linux, zfs-zed,
 zfs-dracut, libpam-zfs, libnvpair3linux, libuutil3linux, libzfs6linux,
 libzfs7linux, libzpool6linux, libzpool7linux, libzfsbootenv1linux,
 libzfslinux-dev
Replaces: zfsutils-linux, zfs-zed, zfs-dracut, libpam-zfs, libnvpair3linux,
 libuutil3linux, libzfs6linux, libzfs7linux, libzpool6linux, libzpool7linux,
 libzfsbootenv1linux, libzfslinux-dev
Description: OpenZFS @ZFSVER@ userspace, the exact version in the FreedomNAS kernel
 zpool, zfs, zed, the libraries, the PAM module and the dracut module of
 OpenZFS @ZFSVER@, built together with linux-image-@KREL@. Stands in for
 Debian's zfsutils-linux, zfs-zed and zfs-dracut, so the userspace can
 never drift from the modules the kernel carries.
